CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ block-scope using-declaration: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [basic.lookup.general]/1, [basic.lookup.unqual]/1-2: unqualified name
lookup stops at the first scope in which a declaration of the name is
found.  For template names the front end kept searching the enclosing
scopes (cpp_scopet::lookup_rec) even past a block scope, and also found the
class template s::is_mi,
so `is_mi<int>(p)' named the class template ("found no match for symbol
'is_mi'", bin53).  libstdc++ 13's ranges::__copy_or_move uses `using
__detail::__is_move_iterator;' (a variable template) while the class
template std::__is_move_iterator is visible, so its body was dropped
(ranges_algobase.h:213) and std::ranges::copy was nondeterministic.  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program (-std=c++98), and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
